I used to dread R's, MF's, MMF's, and L's, and they used to be genocide
targets as soon as I got my grubby hands on a ?oG.

But eventually, I learned how to deal with them, and they aren't as
scary anymore. I actually ascended a genoless character after that. The
main thing is to make sure you always have MR, avoid melee as much as
possible, and think before you move (esp. after feeling the psychic
waves, or right after a summoning storm where you may get an MMF next to
you---this happened to me).

My recent purple worm taming streak made things even more fun: a
sufficiently beefed up purple worm will swallow MF's, MMF's, and all L's
(except master lich, IIRC) with one hit. Heck, a purpworm will even
swallow minotaurs whole. Pet herding techniques are extremely useful
here.


